mode: "100644"
text: "# Facebook Groups 2026 — verified\n\n*Volatile. Re-verify quarterly (Meta ships algorithm + product changes often).*\n\n## The POV: Groups are Facebook's last organic goldmine — community engineering, not broadcasting\n**Pages are dying organically** (~**1.37–1.65%** reach/post). **Groups reach 40–50% of members per post**\n(conservative estimates say 20–40% — either way a **10–30× multiplier**) — a 10k-member group reaches\n**2,000–5,000** vs a Page's ~137–600. **1.8B monthly Group\nusers** across **10M+ active groups**; **700M+ visit Groups daily.** Groups generate **~5× the engagement** of\nPages, members **return 2× as often**, and group audiences **convert at 3–5× cold** (well-managed niche groups\nhit **20–23%** on direct offers; **$3K–15K/mo** is common). **Facebook deliberately favors Groups** (\"Groups\nfor Good\" / community strategy as a counterbalance to messaging apps + rival platforms — expected through\n2027): Group posts outrank Page posts because the **Andromeda AI reads back-and-forth conversation as\n\"meaningful social interaction\" (MSI).** The mindset shift: **\"broadcast marketing\" → \"community\nengineering.\"** A group is a **\"watering hole\"** for your most qualified leads — **value first, trust second,\nsales third** (lead-with-promotion groups fail).\n\n## Setup + structure\n- **Name:** keyword-rich + searchable (\"Social Media Marketing Tips,\" not \"Our Cool Group\"). **Privacy:\n  Private (Visible)** for most — **discoverable in search but content members-only**; private groups see ~40%\n  higher engagement (exclusivity → openness). **Description:** what members get + the rules. **Branded cover**;\n  **tags** for discovery; **2–3 membership questions** to filter quality members (+ capture emails); **admin\n  approval** at first.\n\n## Content + engagement (inside the group)\n- **Two-way conversation, not broadcast** (treating it like a Page kills it). **Post daily** with varied\n  content — educational, discussions, **polls** (one-click engagement that punches above its weight), occasional\n  promos. **Consistency > frequency.** **Short-form video/Reels ~3× the reach** of static; photos high\n  engagement. **Engagement velocity: the first 30–60 min** (10 genuine comments in 30 min reaches 3–5× more\n  than over 24h — notify your most engaged members). **Saves + shares > likes.** **Don't sell in the first 30\n  days**; **never post-and-ghost** (respond, or reach tanks). Sub-groups for scale; automated welcome messages\n  + pinned resources.\n\n## Growth (quality, not blasts)\n- **200–500 members/month** is sustainable + healthy ratios (fast low-quality invite blasts tank reach — big\n  audience, no interaction). **~1,000 members in 2–4 months** with active effort (2–4 weeks with an email\n  list; 6–12 months organic-only). **Levers:** invite your **email list + social followers** (target ~30%\n  acceptance, ~40% 30-day retention), **non-competing admin partnerships** (co-host/giveaways/shout-outs), a\n  **lead magnet**, and **ads to the group join link** (you can't run ads inside a group). **Genuine\n  cross-posting** of value in related groups drives discovery — but **NOT bulk-poster/automation blasting**\n  (ToS violation; Facebook's aggressive AI detection → bans / group removal). **AI content** is treated\n  identically to human content (no penalty) — but low-quality AI spam is detected.\n"
